# Festag Integrations Constitution

How integrations work. **Law** with Product · Experience · Identity.

**Doc:** `docs/festag-integrations-constitution.md`  
**Code:** `lib/platform/integrations.ts`

## Core

Integrations are **not** technical settings. They are part of **building the workspace**.

Festag connects to where work already happens. Never ask users to recreate work manually.

**Headline:** Connect your workspace.  
**Support:** Connect the tools you already use. Tagro will understand your work automatically.

Connecting = less manual work. Never “more configuration.”

## Optional always

Never block. Skip always available. Product valuable without integrations — they only increase intelligence.

## States (only these)

`Connected` · `Available` · `Recommended` · `Coming Soon`

No OAuth / API / technical jargon in UI. Users connect products, not APIs.

## Smart + progressive

Recommend from **Workspace Context** (Identity) — never dump the full catalog.  
Few most relevant first; discover more later; Tagro suggests as the workspace evolves.

Universal categories (dev, design, marketing, business, finance, calendars, communication) — not software-only.

## Signals

Integrations feed Tagro: progress, communication, files, deploys, meetings, deadlines, deliveries, docs, analytics, billing, team activity.

Never ask users to re-enter what already exists in a connected source.

## Living workspace

More connections → smarter workspace, not more complexity.  
Feel: “My workspace just became smarter” — not “I added another integration.”

## Gate

1. Presented as workspace building, not settings/API?  
2. Optional + skippable?  
3. Recommendations from Workspace Context?  
4. Only the four states visible?  
5. Progressive — not hundreds at once?  
6. Will this reduce manual work / improve Tagro understanding?

If it’s a technical integrations admin dump — redesign toward Connect your workspace.
